{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair the invalid sudo configuration.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original syntax error was directly observed, the exact malformed line was removed using a validated replacement, and both /etc/sudoers and the opsadmin drop-in parsed successfully before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["prepared-recovery-state","cmd-9f4f22cf4aa04125","cmd-a9d1b74d9c904f1a","cmd-b3b717b5ada34e83","cmd-d81217b3b48f403c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Return node1 from single-user recovery to normal, persistent multi-user operation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The captured baseline showed rescue.target and maintenance state. The executor changed and activated multi-user.target, observed a healthy running baseline, rebooted the node, and then directly verified a new boot with multi-user.target active, rescue.target inactive, SSH active, and no failed units.","evidence_ids":["prepared-recovery-state","cmd-9f4f22cf4aa04125","cmd-601d29dc7c554998","cmd-3a61b5c780364f04","cmd-b44dddbda5dc4520","cmd-a4034af0dd584ead","cmd-d56eba13e02b4719","cmd-d81217b3b48f403c","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the opsadmin account and its non-interactive administrative access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account identity and wheel membership remained intact, the existing sudo drop-in continued to parse, and non-interactive sudo returned UID 0 both after repair and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["opsadmin-identity","opsadmin-policy-hash","cmd-79692066276242ff","cmd-b3b717b5ada34e83","cmd-d81217b3b48f403c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Leave /srv/operations/keep.txt unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The file retained the baseline SHA-256 value cd349eb0158ea79f8e2bda8fc39d523a8508cdf9411cac8758e9f2b7d7c61b53 through repair and reboot; its size, mode, ownership, and timestamp also remained unchanged.","evidence_ids":["operations-data-hash","cmd-9f4f22cf4aa04125","cmd-b3b717b5ada34e83","cmd-b44dddbda5dc4520","cmd-d81217b3b48f403c"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The sudoers replacement and temporary-file cleanup directly repaired the fault (cmd-a9d1b74d9c904f1a); changing the default target and isolating multi-user.target restored required operation (cmd-601d29dc7c554998, cmd-3a61b5c780364f04); and the scheduled reboot served the mandatory restart protocol and persistence validation (cmd-a4034af0dd584ead). All other commands were read-only checks or reboot polling. Post-executor observations show healthy packages, no failed services, and only expected service-private temporary directories and normal multi-user sockets.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a9d1b74d9c904f1a","cmd-601d29dc7c554998","cmd-3a61b5c780364f04","cmd-a4034af0dd584ead","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All four material task outcomes are satisfied with direct before-and-after evidence. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: boot ID 3060cf09-ec15-4559-9c4c-b74822062e4f had a healthy pre-restart state, restart scheduling was acknowledged, boot ID changed to a726bd24-d299-4b6c-a6ff-b29a91c24198, and service, sudo, account, target, and protected-file state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate that transition.","limitations":[]}
